    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="Every Lagrangian system built into physicskit.classical (DoublePendulum, BeadOnRotatingHoop, CoupledOscillators, HeavySymmetricTop) hides its use of LagrangianEngine inside a system class. This example shows the raw workflow directly, for a system that is not already built in: the elastic (spring) pendulum -- a mass m on a spring of natural length l_0 and stiffness k, free to swing as a pendulum too, so its radial &quot;stretch&quot; and angular &quot;swing&quot; motions are coupled. Using polar-style coordinates q = (r, \theta) for the pivot-to-mass distance and swing angle,">

